{
  "title": "Indian economy grew faster than expected on manufacturing, govt spending",
  "publication_date": "2023-11-29T19:32:00Z",
  "summary": "India's economy demonstrated stronger-than-anticipated growth, driven by robust performance in manufacturing sectors and increased government expenditure. The growth reflects continued economic resilience despite global challenges.",
  "content": "India's economy showed remarkable resilience with faster-than-expected growth rates, primarily supported by strong manufacturing activity and heightened government spending. The expansion was particularly notable in key industrial sectors, with manufacturing showing significant improvement compared to previous quarters. Government capital expenditure and infrastructure investments played a crucial role in driving this growth momentum. The performance indicates India's continuing economic strength amid global economic uncertainties, with domestic consumption and industrial output serving as main growth drivers.\n\nThe growth figures suggest that India remains one of the fastest-growing major economies, maintaining its position as an attractive destination for global investments. The manufacturing sector's revival has been particularly encouraging, showing signs of sustained recovery post-pandemic disruptions.",
